# Sinfonia No. 2 in C minor, BWV 788 (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a gentle, plaintive 12/8 piece with a pastoral, siciliano
# lilt. The subject (C-G-Eb-Eb-C-G-G) opens over a descending bass line;
# long held trilled notes in the top voice (bars 7, 30) frame it. It
# ends with a major third (Picardy) in the last chord.
#
# Tempo: dotted quarter = 60 (four beats a bar). Timings for 32 bars:
# Andras Schiff (clavichord, ECM) 2:08, about 60; Angela Hewitt 1:43,
# about 75; Glenn Gould 3:04, about 42. 60 follows Schiff: unhurried,
# and the lilt survives on plain square waves.
#
# Structure (my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   1-10   C minor: subject top 1, mid 3 (in the tonic), bass head in
#          sequence 5-7; Eb major close at bar 8; cadence in G minor at
#          bar 10 (third beat).
#   9-18   G minor entries: bass 9.5, top 11.5, mid 13.5; cadence in
#          G minor bar 13; episode in F and Eb (14-16) over a held Bb
#          in the bass (15-16).
#   19-27  cadence in G minor at 19; subject top 19-20 turning to
#          F minor, mid 21-22 (flat keys); sequences 23-26.
#   28-32  cadence and return in C minor at 28: bass entry 28, alto
#          29, held trilled C on top 30-31; final cadence bar 32.

tempo 60 4.
rit 1.5 0.7               # last bar and a half: the close onto the major chord
broaden 27 0.93           # bar 27: the cadence that brings back C minor

dyn 1 mp                  # bars 1-10: plaintive opening
dyn 10.5 mf               # bars 10-18: after the G minor cadence, entries in G minor
dyn 19 mp                 # bars 19-27: the darker flat-key middle (F minor, Bb minor)
dyn 28 mf                 # bars 28-32: return to C minor

lead 1-2 top              # subject in the top
lead 3-4 mid              # entry in the middle (tonic)
lead 9.5-10 bottom        # bass entry in G minor
lead 11.5-12 top          # top entry in G minor
lead 13.5-14 mid          # middle entry in G minor
lead 19-20 top            # top entry, turning to F minor
lead 21-22 mid            # middle entry in the flat keys
lead 28 bottom            # bass entry on the return to C minor
